[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2938058674","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107099#issuecomment-2938058674","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107099","id":2938058674,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vHzey","user":{"login":"jcostello","id":1168582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjg1ODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1168582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello","html_url":"https://github.com/jcostello","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jcostello/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T02:00:11Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T02:00:11Z","body":"Quality improves a lot","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2938058674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2938443679","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107099#issuecomment-2938443679","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107099","id":2938443679,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vJRef","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-04T04:28:41Z","updated_at":"2025-06-04T04:28:41Z","body":"In the scene shader we premultiply the light energy by PI to avoid the multiplication in the shader. Basically when everyone moved to PBR, they started multiplying the light energy by PI since the energy-conserving BRDF includes a division by PI. In sky shaders we exposed the light energy directly because we aren't doing a proper PBR BRDF. So we kept what the user gets in the shader in the same units as what they specify on the scene-side. As you have noticed, we use the energy directly in the calculation of sun-scatter. Therefore, I think this is the correct fix. We shouldn't premultiply on the scene side as that would be compatibility breaking. \r\n\r\nDirectional lights in sky:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/1b37dacc1842779fb0d03a5b09026f59c13744fc/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/environment/sky.cpp#L1094-L1096\r\n\r\nDirectional Lights in scene:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/1b37dacc1842779fb0d03a5b09026f59c13744fc/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/storage_rd/light_storage.cpp#L643-L647","author_associat